  "distance_km": 15.0,
  "description": "This walk takes you from the Barnesmore Gap to the Salmon Leap near the town of Ballybofey in east County Donegal. The route starts off at the Barnesmore Gap picnic and parking area a few miles south west of Ballybofey. The walk then heads north, passing Lough Mourne and Garranbane Hill before coming to the Salmon Leap on the River Finn. Here you can see the wild Atlantic salmon climbing the narrow falls at Cloghan as they migrate upstream.Along the way there are some wonderful views of theBluestack Mountainsto enjoy.To the south east you'll find theKilleter Forest Walk. The forest is a good place to extend your walking in the area.Lough Eskecan be found just to the west.",
